---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
const dimensions = [
  {id:'roomWidth',label:'Room width',value:'10',unit:'ft'},
  {id:'roomLength',label:'Room length',value:'12',unit:'ft'},
  {id:'tileWidth',label:'Tile width',value:'12',unit:'in'},
  {id:'tileLength',label:'Tile length',value:'12',unit:'in'},
];
---
<SiteLayout title="2D Tile Layout Planner" description="Explore a scaled rectangular tile layout. Compare corner and centered grids, rotate tiles, and see edge cuts before reviewing your purchase estimate.">
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="py-10 sm:py-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Plan smarter. Tile with confidence.</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[40px] font-bold leading-[1.08] tracking-[-0.045em] sm:text-[56px]">Tile Layout Planner<span class="text-teal">.</span></h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-muted sm:text-lg">Find your starting point. Explore a straight tile grid, compare balanced edges, and see where cuts will fall.</p>
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-xs text-muted sm:text-sm">{['True room proportions','Full tiles & edge cuts','US & metric units'].map(label=><span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="rounded-full bg-[#dff1f3] p-1 text-teal"><Icon name="check" size={13}/></span>{label}</span>)}</div>
    </section>
    <div class="grid items-start gap-5 lg:grid-cols-[380px_minmax(0,1fr)]">
      <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="settings-title">
        <h2 id="settings-title" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Layout settings</h2><p class="mt-1 mb-6 text-sm text-muted">Adjust a measurement. See the plan change.</p>
        <form id="layout-form" novalidate>
          {['Room size','Tile size'].map((section,index)=><fieldset class="mb-6"><legend class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold">{section}</legend><div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">{dimensions.slice(index*2,index*2+2).map(field=><div><label class="field-label" for={field.id}>{field.label}</label><div class="field-shell"><input id={field.id} class="field-input" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value={field.value} required/><select id={`${field.id}-unit`} class="field-unit max-w-18" aria-label={`${field.label} unit`}>{['ft','in','m','cm','mm'].map(unit=><option value={unit} selected={unit===field.unit}>{unit}</option>)}</select></div></div>)}</div></fieldset>)}
          <div class="mb-6"><label class="field-label" for="grout">Grout spacing</label><div class="field-shell max-w-44"><input id="grout" class="field-input" inputmode="decimal" type="text" value="2" required aria-describedby="grout-hint"/><span class="field-unit">mm</span></div><p id="grout-hint" class="helper">0–25 mm; less than each tile dimension. Follow your tile manufacturer’s specifications.</p></div>
          <fieldset class="mb-6"><legend class="mb-3 text-sm font-bold">Layout options</legend><div class="space-y-4"><div><label class="field-label" for="orientation">Tile orientation</label><select id="orientation" class="field-input rounded-lg border border-line bg-[#f7f9fb]"><option value="0">Straight · 0°</option><option value="90">Rotated · 90°</option></select></div><div><label class="field-label" for="start">Starting point</label><select id="start" class="field-input rounded-lg border border-line bg-[#f7f9fb]"><option value="corner">Top-left corner</option><option value="center">Centered · equal opposite edges</option></select></div></div></fieldset>
          <details class="rounded-lg border border-line p-3"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-semibold">Purchase estimate inputs</summary><p class="helper mb-3">Carried over from the calculator. These do not change the drawing.</p><div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3"><div><label class="field-label text-xs" for="waste">Allowance (%)</label><input id="waste" class="field-input rounded-lg border border-line" inputmode="decimal" value="10"/></div><div><label class="field-label text-xs" for="tilesPerBox">Tiles per box</label><input id="tilesPerBox" class="field-input rounded-lg border border-line" inputmode="numeric" value="10"/></div><div class="col-span-2"><label class="field-label text-xs" for="pricePerBox">Box price (USD, optional)</label><input id="pricePerBox" class="field-input rounded-lg border border-line" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="0.00"/></div></div></details>
          <p id="layout-error" class="mt-4 rounded-lg bg-red-50 p-3 text-sm text-red-800" role="alert" hidden></p>
          <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-t border-line pt-4"><button type="reset" class="btn-secondary"><Icon name="reset" size={16}/>Reset</button><button type="submit" class="btn-primary px-4">View layout<Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></button></div>
        </form>
      </section>
      <div class="min-w-0 space-y-5">
        <section id="layout-preview" tabindex="-1" class="panel bg-[#f1f8fa]" aria-labelledby="preview-title">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h2 id="preview-title" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Your 2D floor plan</h2><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">Top view · automatically fits your room</p></div><span class="rounded-full bg-white px-3 py-1 text-[10px] font-bold tracking-wider text-teal">LIVE PREVIEW</span></div>
          <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs text-muted"><span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="size-4 rounded-sm border border-[#718c96] bg-[#e1e9e7]"></span>Full tile</span><span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="size-4 rounded-sm border border-dashed border-teal bg-[#a8d9db]"></span>Cut piece</span><span>White gaps = grout</span></div>
          <div id="drawing" class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[#e0eaee] bg-white p-1 sm:p-3"><p class="p-10 text-center text-sm text-muted">Your plan will appear here when JavaScript is enabled.</p></div>
          <p id="layout-status" class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted" aria-live="polite">Enter your dimensions to explore the layout.</p>
          <dl class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs"><div class="rounded-lg bg-white p-3"><dt class="text-muted">Left / right piece width</dt><dd id="edge-x" class="mt-1 font-semibold">—</dd></div><div class="rounded-lg bg-white p-3"><dt class="text-muted">Top / bottom piece height</dt><dd id="edge-y" class="mt-1 font-semibold">—</dd></div></dl>
        </section>
        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h2 id="summary-title" class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">Planning summary</h2><button id="compare-start" type="button" class="btn-secondary px-0 text-xs">Try centered edges <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></button></div>
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">{[['full','Full tiles'],['cut','Cut pieces'],['area','Room area'],['boxes','Est. boxes']].map(([key,label])=><div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-3"><p class="text-[11px] font-medium text-muted">{label}</p><p id={`summary-${key}`} class="mt-2 break-words text-xl font-bold">—</p></div>)}</div>
          <p id="purchase-note" class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">Purchase quantities use the calculator’s area-based method.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 rounded-lg bg-[#edf6f7] p-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="text-ink">Pieces are not a shopping list.</strong> A cut piece may share a source tile with another cut. This tool does not optimize cutting or calculate a minimum purchase quantity.</p>
          <a id="open-calculator" class="btn-primary mt-5 w-full" href="/calculator/">Review purchase estimate <Icon name="arrow" size={18}/></a>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 p-5 text-sm">Enable JavaScript to generate a layout. The explanation below remains available without it.</p></noscript>
    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 border-t border-line pt-9 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">A clear starting point</p><h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">How this grid is defined</h2><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted"><strong class="text-ink">Corner:</strong> the first tile starts at the top-left wall. Full tiles and grout repeat toward the right and bottom. If a wall falls inside a grout joint, the remaining grout strip is reported below the drawing.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted"><strong class="text-ink">Centered:</strong> each axis uses the fewest pieces that span the room, with equal cuts at opposite walls and full tiles in between. An exact fit stays uncut. If one tile covers an axis, it is clipped to that room dimension. This can place either a tile or a grout joint on the centerline.</p></div>
      <div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">A planning aid, before the dry layout</h2><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">The plan supports one rectangular room and a straight grid at 0° or 90°. Tile dimensions are the material size, with grout added between pieces. No additional perimeter movement gap is included. Dimensions are rounded for display; the geometry and purchase calculation retain exact inputs.</p><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted">The preview draws up to 2,500 pieces. Larger valid plans show the room outline and numerical summary. Irregular rooms, diagonal patterns, herringbone, cutting optimization and installation details are outside this tool’s scope. Check the actual room, tile size, joint specifications and edge cuts with your installer before cutting or ordering.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm"><a class="font-semibold text-teal underline underline-offset-4" href="/guides/how-to-measure-a-room-for-tile/">Start with accurate room measurements →</a></p><p class="mt-3 text-sm"><a class="font-semibold text-teal underline underline-offset-4" href="/guides/tile-layout-starting-point/">Compare corner and centered layouts →</a></p></div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
<script>import '../../scripts/layout';</script>
